{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start the process for ACME, begin with the New Resupply Cycle and then Check Levels of Inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Initial structural node and three sequential actions directly paraphrase the opening sequence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n5",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the inventory is below or equal to the minimum, generate an Equal to or below minimum Report. If the inventory is greater than the minimum, generate an Above Minimum Report."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards capture the two inventory conditions; actions capture the corresponding report generations. Variable abstraction in guards preserves decision logic."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->c_loop",
        "guard:b2->c_end_path",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the report indicates that the inventory is equal to or below the minimum, create Purchase Orders (POs). If the report indicates that the inventory is above the minimum, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch splits based on report outcome. Positive path creates POs; negative path ends process. Guards use Yes/No abstraction but preserve branching logic."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n11",
        "guard:b3->n13",
        "action:n11",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the PO is rejected, it needs to be reworked. If the PO is approved, it is printed and released in the system."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards model approval/rejection logic; actions perform rework or print/release accordingly."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed. If the PO needs to be reworked, it needs to be created again."
      ],
      "justification": "Review step is modeled explicitly. Loop-back convergence handles the 'created again' requirement without changing behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20",
        "action:n21"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, reserve funds for the released POs and mail the POs to the supplier."
      ],
      "justification": "AND gateway models simultaneous execution; actions match funding and mailing steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n22",
        "action:n23",
        "action:n24",
        "action:n25"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If funds are reserved for the released POs, receive the Packing Slip. If the POs are mailed to the supplier, receive the inventory. If the Packing Slip is received, proceed to receive the Invoice. If the inventory is received, proceed to receive the Packing Slip. If the Invoice is received, proceed to the Three-way match."
      ],
      "justification": "Convergence joins parallel branches; subsequent actions sequence the receipt of slip, inventory, invoice, and three-way match preparation. Overall behavioural flow is preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n26",
        "action:n28"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the Three-way match is successful, release the funds. Once the funds are released, issue the payment. After the payment is issued, the Resupply Cycle is complete and the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Final sequence of fund release, payment issuance, and process termination matches the source exactly."
    }
  ],
